{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_007: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted fusion → 52.3% acc, 0.87 GPU-hr), the most critical uncertainty is whether moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with aggregation meaningfully improves performance. config_010 is the cleanest controlled extension of config_007: it keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), the same image encoder (resnet50), and the same fusion strategy (weighted), changing only the profile setting to multiprofile and adding avgpool aggregation. This isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation as the single variable. If accuracy improves, it validates the multiprofile direction and justifies investing remaining budget in stronger encoders (scgpt, ViT-L) or transformer aggregation on top of it. If it does not improve, it tells us singleprofile is sufficient and we should pivot to encoder upgrades. The expected cost is modestly higher than config_007 (~1.0–1.3 GPU-hr) due to multiprofile processing, but avgpool is a cheap aggregation, so the overhead is limited. Under an 8-experiment remaining budget, this controlled comparison is the highest-information-per-GPU-hour next step."
}

